      'Digital marketing and direct-to-consumer selling skills matter as much here as anywhere else - the craft is genuine, but the business model around it usually is not modernised',
      'For those leaving the craft entirely, the same high-value skill portfolio logic applies as anywhere else: proof of work, market positioning, and a deliberate skill choice rather than a default',
    ],
  },
];

const craftSummaryItems = [
  {
    title: 'Tradition versus modern career is a real tension here, not a talking point',
    body: 'The honest answer is rarely "abandon the craft" or "only the craft." It is usually a specific choice between modernising the same trade with new skills, or building a different high-value skill path while the family craft continues in the background.',
